   "id": "typical",
   "title": "Figure 2-1. Typical application",
   "page": 4,
   "description": "The supervisor shares the microcontroller's supply. Its reset output goes straight to the microcontroller's MCLR (reset) input, holding it in reset until VDD is above the trip point plus the timeout, and again whenever VDD drops below it. A bypass capacitor sits across the supervisor's VDD and ground. The MCP100 is shown, for a microcontroller with an active-low reset input.",
